    "narrative": "The **Gunnar Henderson** matchup against Holmes represents the clear headliner for the Austin Waves today, commanding an elite 81.87 score. His heavy weight in the 3-hole combined with an advantageous 4.75 xERA matchup and a significant 14% platoon edge creates a massive ceiling for run production. Behind him, **Drake Baldwin** (71.82) is a prioritized start due to the leadoff spot and a 16% park factor boost, while **Jackson Merrill** (68.50) and **Sam Antonacci** (67.67) capitalize on high-SB upside. Both **Jackson Merrill** and **Nasim Nunez** (62.14) are further bolstered by the slow deliveries of their opposing pitchers, which we are heavily leveraging to address our need for stolen base volume.\n\nThe most difficult exclusion today was **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, who missed the cut at 54.40. While he benefits from the same favorable matchup against Rodriguez as **Nasim Nunez**, his efficiency was hampered by a 15% penalty for platoon disadvantage and a suboptimal batting order placement. We opted for **Curtis Mead** in the UTIL slot despite his own platoon headwinds, as his broader path to counting stats marginally edged out **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**'s current projection. We are also closely monitoring **Heliot Ramos**; while his 66.52 score is solid, the wind-out conditions provide a slight variance buffer that makes him one of our more volatile contributors. With **Kyle Tucker** facing a tougher matchup against Manaea (3.80 xERA), he sits in a lower-tier efficiency slot today, serving as a reminder that we must prioritize category-specific speed and high-leverage spots to maintain our 5x5 pace.",
